SEG = 'COD'
CAT = 'ftasCode'
Q = [
    ("A family member is in a mental health crisis. Tasmania Police says the safest choice for the firearms is to:",
     "Store them away from home", ["Hide them in the garage roof", "Keep them unloaded at home", "Sell them the same day"],
     "Information Sheet 4 says storing firearms away from the home temporarily is the safest choice when someone may be at risk."),
    ("Firearms are moved to a relative's home during a crisis. That relative must:",
     "Hold the right licence", ["Be at least 25 years old", "Live in the same town", "Own a separate gun room"],
     "Tasmania Police says the relative or friend must have a firearms licence of the relevant category and be able to store the firearms as the regulations require."),
    ("Which option does Tasmania Police list for storing firearms away from home during a crisis?",
     "Temporary surrender to police", ["A locked car boot at work", "A rented storage garage", "An unlicensed friend's shed"],
     "Information Sheet 4 lists a licensed relative or friend, a firearms dealer for a fee, or temporary surrender to police until the crisis has passed."),
    ("If the firearms must stay at home during a crisis, one step Tasmania Police suggests is to:",
     "Change the safe's combination", ["Leave the safe unlocked", "Keep just one rifle loaded", "Hang the key by the door"],
     "Information Sheet 4 suggests keeping keys away from the person at risk, changing the combination, storing a key part away, and removing ammunition."),
    ("Why does Tasmania Police say delaying access to a firearm helps in a suicidal crisis?",
     "It buys time to reconsider", ["It makes guns harder to clean", "It satisfies the insurer", "It lowers registration fees"],
     "Information Sheet 4 says a crisis can escalate quickly but the impulse is usually short-lived, so anything that delays access gives the person time."),
    ("Tasmania Police says a suicidal crisis may escalate faster with:",
     "Alcohol or drug use", ["A recent licence renewal", "A change to daylight saving", "Buying a new firearm"],
     "Information Sheet 4 notes that experts identify acute intoxication with alcohol or drugs as able to contribute to rapid escalation."),
    ("You suspect your old shotgun has a mechanical defect. Tasmania Police suggests contacting:",
     "Firearms Services or a dealer", ["The Department of Natural Resources", "Staff at Service Tasmania", "The captain of a rifle club"],
     "Information Sheet 4 says to contact Firearms Services or a firearms dealer, as many dealers can assess whether a firearm is safe and repair it."),
    ("A Tasmanian licence expired and no renewal was lodged by midnight on the 14th day. The holder must:",
     "Surrender their firearms", ["Keep them until renewal", "Lend them to a licensee", "Store them at a dealer free"],
     "Firearms Services says that if the renewal is not lodged by midnight on the 14th day after expiry, the holder must surrender their firearms and can only make a new application."),
    ("To slow access during a crisis, Tasmania Police suggests storing which part away from home?",
     "The bolt or slide", ["The carry sling", "The scope caps", "The cleaning rod and kit"],
     "Information Sheet 4 suggests storing a key component, like the slide or bolt, separately or away from the home, so the firearm cannot be fired quickly."),
    ("After a renewal, the earliest a new Tasmanian licence card arrives is how long before the old card expires?",
     "21 days before", ["The day it expires", "90 days before", "6 months before"],
     "Firearms Services says the earliest you will receive a new licence card is 21 days before your current card's expiry date, and the new licence starts when the old one ends."),
    ("The Code's explanation of rule 8 says a parked vehicle is:",
     "Not secure storage", ["Fine for one night", "Safe if alarmed", "Better than a safe"],
     "The Code says vehicles should not be considered a secure option in which to store your firearms."),
    ("What is the only genuine reason Tasmania Police accepts for possessing imitation firearms?",
     "Collection", ["Target shooting", "Film work", "Home display"],
     "Firearms Services says the only genuine reason to possess imitation or replica firearms is collection, under a licence of the appropriate category."),
    ("You are flying interstate with your rifle. The Code advises you to:",
     "Contact the airline early", ["Pack it in your hand luggage", "Mail it ahead to the hotel", "Remove the barrel only"],
     "The Code advises contacting the airline well before departure to find out how it requires firearms to be submitted for transport."),
    ("Unlike real firearms, imitation firearms in Tasmania do not have to be:",
     "Registered", ["Stored securely", "Licensed", "Kept unloaded"],
     "Firearms Services says imitation firearms need not be registered, but every other provision of the Act, including safekeeping and storage, applies as if they were real."),
    ("What makes an item an imitation firearm rather than a toy, according to Tasmania Police?",
     "Its size and features", ["Its bright colour alone", "Its retail price", "Where it was bought"],
     "Firearms Services says it is the size and features of the item that make it an imitation, not its colour; if it could reasonably be taken for a firearm, it is an imitation."),
    ("In Tasmania, buying a chassis kit, stock or rail for a rifle needs:",
     "No authorisation needed", ["A permit to acquire", "A firearms dealer licence", "A Category H licence"],
     "Firearms Services says chassis kits, conversion kits, stocks, rails and grips are not firearm parts and are not specifically regulated, though fitting them may change a firearm's legal status."),
    ("The Code describes head space as the distance between the bolt face and:",
     "The cartridge base", ["The muzzle crown", "The front sight", "The trigger guard"],
     "The Code lists head space, the distance between the base of the chambered cartridge and the face of the bolt, among parts needing a gunsmith's attention."),
    ("You are taking a rifle out of a car boot. The Code says to remove it:",
     "Butt first", ["Muzzle first", "By the sling", "By the barrel"],
     "Under rule 14, the Code warns that people have shot themselves or companions by removing a firearm muzzle first."),
    ("Where does the Code say you should check a firearm's action using ammunition?",
     "A safe place like a range", ["In your locked garage", "In the back yard at dusk", "Inside the open gun safe"],
     "The Code says never to check the action with ammunition at home; test firing in or around the home, even on rural land, is not safe."),
    ("Your cartridges got wet on a hunting trip. The Code says you must never:",
     "Dry them in an oven", ["Leave them to air dry", "Wipe them with a cloth", "Return them to the box"],
     "The Code warns never to dry wet or damp ammunition in an oven, a microwave or in front of a fire, as it may cause an explosion."),
    ("A chassis kit takes a pistol's overall length past 65 cm. Tasmania Police warns that:",
     "It may leave Category H", ["It becomes Category A", "Nothing changes at all", "It must be re-registered"],
     "Firearms Services warns that if a pistol is no longer one-handed or is longer than 65 cm, it may no longer be a Category H firearm, and other changes can make it a prohibited pistol."),
    ("You no longer want your registered shotgun. Besides surrendering it to police, Tasmania Police says you may:",
     "Sell it via a dealer", ["Give it to a licensed friend", "Bury it on your land", "Put it in council waste"],
     "Firearms Services says to dispose of a firearm or ammunition you must sell it to or through a licensed dealer or surrender it to police."),
    ("An athletics club wants to use a starting pistol at meets. Firearms Services says it may seek:",
     "An exemption", ["A Category H licence", "A dealer licence", "No paperwork"],
     "Firearms Services lists people using starting pistols and similar devices at sporting events among those who have been issued exemptions under the Act."),
    ("You plan to zero a rifle on a rural property. The Code suggests first:",
     "Telling the neighbours", ["Firing at night", "Using a metal plate", "Shooting towards a dam"],
     "The Code says a few minutes talking to neighbours before zeroing on a rural property is good manners and reduces the stress gunshots can cause."),
]
